==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Same as Estonian [[#Estonian|kivi]].

===Pronunciation===
*Hyphenation: ki·vi
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:Finnish:-iʋi|-iʋi]]
*{{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkiʋi]}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun|kiv|type=pilvi}}

# A [[stone]]
# Any piece of [[stone]] which is larger than a grain of sand.
# A [[rock]] as a relatively small mass of stone projecting out of ground.
# A general term for solid, mineral-based construction materials, such as [[brick]], [[concrete]] or natural stone.
# {{colloquial|lang=fi}} An underwater [[rock]] which bay be dangerous for seafarers; same as ''[[kari]]''.
# A short form of ''[[jalokivi]]'', or a [[jewel]].
#:''Tässä kellossa on 17 kiveä'' = This clockwork is made with 17 jewels.

